-- =============================================================================
-- Demo seed, local profile and integration tests only (spring.flyway.locations adds classpath:db/demo there).
--
-- Replaces the ten versioned demo migrations and the no-op repeatable R__demo_catalog_selling_prices that ran
-- interleaved with the production ones up to V20261113000610; they could not survive the squash into
-- V20261111000000__baseline, which sorts after most of them. This is the end state they left: the HCM warehouse and
-- its map, the two demo products (SOFA-3S-GREY, TABLE-OAK-160) with their stock in LPN cartons, the demo staff and
-- customer accounts, the truck carrier. It holds only rows the demo seed added; nothing in the baseline is changed.
--
-- Made by pg_dump --data-only of exactly those rows, from a database migrated with the old db/migration + db/demo.
--
-- Triggers are off while it loads: the rows are a snapshot of what the triggers themselves produced (cartons
-- opened by stock rows, inventory items made by variants, ledger lines), so firing them again would double what is
-- already here, and two foreign-key cycles (product.categories, product.variants) cannot be ordered. That needs a
-- superuser - which the local Postgres of docker-compose.yml and Testcontainers both are, and why this location
-- must never be added to a shared environment.
-- =============================================================================

SET LOCAL session_replication_role = replica;

